  "title": "Unified Title",
  "summary": "UniT (Unified Latent Action Tokenizer via Visual Anchoring) and HumanVerse represent a new approach to human-to-humanoid coordination through joint action and motion representations. UniT enables scalable humanoid policy learning while preserving human-to-human transfer, while HumanVerse provides a robust dataset for real-world loco-manipulation tasks.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "UniT introduces a framework for human-to-humanoid transfer with a tri-branch cross-reconstruction mechanism.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "HumanVerse provides a 500-hour dataset for open-world human loco-manipulation, validated for real-world tasks.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Both UniT and HumanVerse demonstrate improved performance in both policy learning and real-world applications.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
